@luke-yuan , First thing first ;
* Name of your only file has to be `hello-world.md` only and it should be placed only in folder `submit-a-pull-request/<username>`.

On investigation of each commit now I found that my above comment wouldn't work as you have made two different hello-world.md file, one in right place and another outside the folder with your username, and now it seems you have created another file with `hello_world.md` but since to complete this task we only want file to be inside the folder of your username and its name should be exactly `hello-world.md`.

So can you delete all the commits by you except first one(you can delete commits by you by following this guide https://zulip.readthedocs.io/en/latest/git/fixing-commits.html#deleting-old-commits)

And then in hello-world.md file simply replace your username with `username` and amend the first commit by using command `git commit --amend` and then add a period (`.`) at the end of the first commit message in window that will pop-up, as asked in the first commit message. There you have your first commit done, now you have to follow the task for the second commit.

 It would be better to make all these changes in a terminal, In case of any problem feel free to reach us at https://chat.zulip.org/#narrow/stream/GCI.20help

