Since ILookup is something like "ReadOnlyMultiValueDictionary" , I suggest that MultiValueDictionary inherits ILookup.
```csharp
public class MultiValueDictionary<TKey, TValue> :
        IReadOnlyDictionary<TKey, IReadOnlyCollection<TValue>>,
        ILookup<TKey, TValue>
{

   IEnumerator<IGrouping<TKey, TValue>> IEnumerable<IGrouping<TKey, TValue>>.GetEnumerator()
        => dictionary.Values.GetEnumerator(); 
   bool ILookup<TKey, TValue>.Contains(TKey key) => ContainsKey(key);

   private class InnerCollectionView :
            ICollection<TValue>,
            IReadOnlyCollection<TValue>,
            IGrouping<TKey,TValue>
   {
   }
// no other change
}
```

pull_request.body:
If you only want to test if a variable contains a specific character, you should use `strpos()` instead of `preg_match()`.

**Before**

```php
<?php

if (preg_match("/abc/", $var)) { // UnneededRegularExpression: Using `strpos()` instead of `preg_match()` will be faster.
    something($var);
}
```

**After**

```php
<?php

if (strpos($var, "abc") !== false) {
    something($var);
}
```

This tool finds a call to `preg_match()` that uses unneeded regular expressions.

