comment.body:
@Lofesa -- I don't think relative vs absolute is critical here, it should be OK to be protocol relative.  

@chaihongjun -- Otto indicated you need to use the CA certificates, and you said you set the cert to your *server* certificates.  Those are not the same thing.  I realize this is confusing, but mod_pagespeed's Serf fetcher is acting as a client, not as a server.  it should be configured based on your host operating system's view of the certificate authority chain, not your server's certificate.

You might also want to consider simplifying your configuration significantly -- copy the current config with all these features to a temporary file, and turn on only (say) image optimization and cache extension, and the HTTPS setup.  Once that's working really well, you can start adding features from your larger config.

commits.message:
powerpc/mm: restore SEGV_ACCERR for segv on mapped region

A recent refactoring of the powerpc page fault handler caused
access to protected memory regions to indicate SEGV_MAPERR instead
of the traditional SEGV_ACCERR in the si_code field of a user-space
signal handler.  This can confuse debug libraries that temporarily
change the protection of memory regions, and expect to use
SEGV_ACCERR as an indication to restore access to a region.

This change restores the previous behavior.  The following program
exhibits the issue:

    $ ./repro read  || echo "FAILED"
    $ ./repro write || echo "FAILED"
    $ ./repro exec  || echo "FAILED"

    #include <stdio.h>
    #include <stdlib.h>
    #include <string.h>
    #include <unistd.h>
    #include <signal.h>
    #include <sys/mman.h>
    #include <assert.h>

    static void segv_handler(int n, siginfo_t *info, void *arg) {
            _exit(info->si_code == SEGV_ACCERR ? 0 : 1);
    }

    int main(int argc, char **argv)
    {
            void *p = NULL;
            struct sigaction act = {
                    .sa_sigaction = segv_handler,
                    .sa_flags = SA_SIGINFO,
            };

            assert(argc == 2);
            p = mmap(NULL, getpagesize(),
                    (strcmp(argv[1], "write") == 0) ? PROT_READ : 0,
                    MAP_PRIVATE|MAP_ANONYMOUS, -1, 0);
            assert(p != MAP_FAILED);

            assert(sigaction(SIGSEGV, &act, NULL) == 0);
            if (strcmp(argv[1], "read") == 0)
                    printf("%c", *(unsigned char *)p);
            else if (strcmp(argv[1], "write") == 0)
                    *(unsigned char *)p = 0;
            else if (strcmp(argv[1], "exec") == 0)
                    ((void (*)(void))p)();
            return 1;  /* failed to generate SEGV */
    }

Signed-off-by: John Sperbeck <jsperbeck@google.com>

Update Gnocchi metrics docs

Update docs:

- metrics ListOpts struct inline documentation;
- metrics Metric struct inline documentation;

